# Tournament leaderboard points — an ExactOdds casino rule pack.
#
# Tournament standings are prize money by another name, so the scoring
# formula has to be one program, not a spreadsheet someone edited. This is
# the formula every entrant sees before they buy in: points scale with the
# field size and fall off with finishing place. Same entrants, same place,
# same points — on every seat, or the program refuses to compile.
#
# Rules: points = entrants * 100 / place, integer division floors. First
# place in a 100-player field scores 10,000; last place scores 100. Ties
# split by the tournament's own tiebreak, applied to the same program.

def tourney_points(place: int, entrants: int) -> int do
    ret entrants * 100 / place
end

# Audited cases.
say(tourney_points(1, 100))
say(tourney_points(10, 100))
say(tourney_points(100, 100))
say(tourney_points(3, 64))
